  The `.cargo_vcs_info.json` records sha `21926a05b797a5ba3b0f42d32207389957af4e12` with
  `path_in_vcs: "color-print"`. This commit exists upstream at gitlab.com/dajoha/color-print
  with message "Release v0.3.7".
  
  - All files in `src/`: **bit-for-bit identical** between tarball and upstream at this sha.
  - `Cargo.toml.orig` vs upstream `Cargo.toml`: **identical**.
  
  **Conclusion:** Source matches upstream exactly. Verification passes.
  
  ## Code review findings
  
  **Thoroughness level: high** (272 LoC Rust across 4 files; every file read in full,
  every line examined.)
  
  **Claims baseline:** Compile-time terminal colorization macros using HTML-like tags.
  The actual parsing happens in the companion proc-macro crate `color-print-proc-macro`;
  this crate re-exports those macros and optionally provides runtime terminfo support.
  
  ### Non-negotiable checks
  
  - **build.rs**: None. Positive.
  - **Proc macros**: Not a proc-macro crate itself; re-exports from `color-print-proc-macro`.
  - **Dependencies**: `color-print-proc-macro` (required, same author), `lazy_static` and
    `terminfo` (optional, behind `terminfo` feature). All justified.
