  default implementations that fall back to max/min/zero on overflow. Comprehensive tests.
  
  src/internal.rs (read in full, 257 lines): Sealed trait implementation. Min/max values computed
  lazily via LazyLock using a binary-search algorithm (starts at 10^18s, halves on failure, terminates
  at 1ns). Clean and correct. Platform-specific tests verify expected Unix values.
  
  Minor notes: unreachable!() in Instant::checked_duration_since is safe due to sealed trait
  override pattern. Instant::anchor() uses now() which is inherent to Instant's design.
  
