    2. Splits on `.` and rejects empty labels, labels > 63 chars, labels starting
       or ending with `-`.
    3. Rejects empty hostnames and hostnames > 253 chars.
  - **No unsafe code.** No `unsafe` blocks anywhere.
  - **No I/O, no network, no filesystem access.** Pure computation on a `&str`.
  - **No macros, no proc-macros, no build script.** Nothing executes at build time.
  - **No panics in non-test code.** All operations are infallible on `&str`/`u8`.
  - **Correctness note:** The function accepts hostnames starting or ending with `.`
    only if the split produces non-empty labels — but `"invalid.name."` is correctly
    rejected by the test (trailing `.` produces an empty label via `split('.')`).
    Leading `.` similarly produces an empty label. This is correct.
  - **Correctness note:** `".invalid"` starts with `.`, and `split('.')` yields
    `["", "invalid"]` — the empty label causes rejection. Verified correct.
  - **Minor doc typo:** Line 28 says "lables" instead of "labels". Cosmetic only.
  - **Test coverage:** Tests cover valid hostnames (mixed case, numeric, dotted) and
    invalid hostnames (leading/trailing `-`, special chars, leading/trailing `.`,
    oversized label, empty label). Reasonable coverage for this scope.
  
